  conflict → Judging it wasteful, the magistrates wanted to demolish the dōjō, using the land for more mundane purposes. They considered [deity0_name]'s ways to be obsolete.
  founderJoin → [founderName], a scholar and master of the martial arts, gathered [founderName_possessive] followers around, and asked them to show the ways of [deity0_name] to the magistrates, preaching their truth by example. They'd show them that only a life lived with honour, courage and skill is worth living.
  victory → The magistrates were humbled by the incredible display of virtue, and their hearts were changed. [founderName] gained great acclaim and [founderName_possessive] teachings spread across the stars.
  setup → [founderName] was a renowned martial artist in one of the Glitterworlds. [founder_pronoun] posited that only a life lived with honour, courage and skill is worth living. By setting one's heart right every morning and evening, he gains freedom in the Way. His whole life will be without blame, and he will succeed in his calling.
  story → Seeking inner peace, [founderName] gathered [founderName_possessive] followers and chartered a ship to travel to the Rim.
  lessonIntro → It is thus that we learn one single truth: "you must live being true to the single purpose of the present moment". The most important thing I've learned is that
  lesson → only a life lived with honour, courage and skill is worth living
  lessonReinforcement → The best fighter is never angry.
  archistBasis → The archotechs are ascended beings, free of the basic instincts that plague humanity.
  archistFact → As supreme ethical beings, the archotechs show us that only a life lived with honour, courage and skill is worth living.
  archistProphecy → [inTheEnd], only those warriors who are pure of heart will be allowed to transcend.
  animistBasis → There are many spirits of War, but the greatest among them all is the spirit of honour.
  animistFact → The greatest among the spirits teaches us that only a life lived with honour, courage and skill is worth living.
  animistProphecy → [itIsSaid] only those warriors who are pure of heart can truly appease the spirits.
  serketistProphecy → [itIsSaid] we will understand that insects teach us that only a life lived with honour, courage and skill is worth living.
  chthonianProphecy → They are the epitome of iniquity. Innately evil, immoral. They are a dark mirror that shows us that only a life lived with honour, courage and skill is worth living.
  esotericismProphecy → Such occult knowledge can't be acquired through dishonourable means, for only a life lived with honour, courage and skill is worth living.
  eschatologismFact → Through the very end, we will keep ourselves pure, for only a life lived with honour, courage and skill is worth living.
  introMemo → Remember our motto! "Only a life lived with honour, courage and skill is worth living". We encourage printing this on stickers to decorate your offices.
  alienistProphecy → These wayward creatures, forgotten and discarded creations of humanity's hubris, remind us that only a life lived with honour, courage and skill is worth living.
